  "name": "pairwise_cost_gap_preference_loss",
  "intuition": "This loss encourages the model to prefer higher-quality outputs by penalizing pairs with larger cost gaps, scaled by their log probabilities. It promotes consistent ranking where better outputs (lower cost) are assigned higher likelihoods, aligning with preference learning objectives in RL4CO.",
  "pseudocode": "loss = mean over pairs of max(0, cost_b - cost_a + margin) * weight * exp(log_prob_w - log_prob_l)",
